  "limitations": [
    "Ethereum EOA scalar derivation only; no ENS, contract derivation or chain-specific checksums",
    "Legacy -m paths retain their CPU behavior; vanity/minikeys/other modes remain pending",
    "No Ethereum throughput, multi-device scaling, calibration, tuning, partition or MIG certification claim",
    "Coordinator acceptance uses isolated localhost mTLS on each validation host; no public deployment"
  ],
  "findings": [
    "Keccak suffix 0x01 and X||Y serialization independently differ from SHA3 and SEC1-prefixed hashing",
    "Uniform hex case remains accepted; mixed case requires ERC-55; all equivalent inputs canonicalize to 20-byte targets",
    "One address per scalar bounds output; target count never bounds the number of hash preimages",
    "Ethereum requires an explicit fourth capability before allocation, renewal, update or cached receipt replay",
    "CPU and GPU hash implementations are separate, and pinned PyCryptodome supplies the third-party test oracle",
    "GPU family translation units remain separate while scalar checkpoint ownership and recovery are shared"
  ],
  "evidence_policy": "Phased acceptance: each log identifies its source phase; embedded binary hashes identify test artifacts. Final binaries are not claimed identical to earlier algorithm-test binaries. Archive excludes credential contents and databases."
